\Rightarrow\quad y^{\prime}(t) &amp;=k x(t) y(t) \Rightarrow \frac{y^{\prime}(t)}{y(t)}=k x(t)\\
\Rightarrow\quad \frac{y^{\prime}(t)}{y(t)} &amp;=k x(t) \Rightarrow \frac{d}{dt}\left[\ln y(t)\right]=k x(t) \Rightarrow \frac{d}{dt}\left[\ln y(t)\right]=\frac{k x(t)}{1}=\frac{k}{1} x(t)\\
\Rightarrow\quad \frac{d}{dt}\left[\ln y(t)\right] &amp;=k \quad \Rightarrow \ln y(t)=kt+C \quad \Rightarrow y(t)=e^{kt+C} \quad \Rightarrow y(t)=A e^{kt}
\end{align*} where $A=e^{C}$. We know that $y(0)=160$, so $A=160$, and we have $y(t)=160 e^{kt}$. We also know that $y(7)=1200$, so $1200=160 e^{7 k}$ and $7 k=\ln (1200 / 160)=\ln (7.5)$, and so $k=\ln (7.5) / 7$. Then $y(t)=160 e^{\ln (7.5) t / 7}$ and $y(t)=160\left(\frac{7.5}{7}\right)^{t / 7}$. We want to find $t$ such that $y(t)=0.2(5000)=1000$, so $1000=160\left(\frac{7.5}{7}\right)^{t / 7}$. Thus, we have $\left(\frac{7.5}{7}\right)^{t / 7}=\frac{1000}{160}$ and $\left(\frac{7.5}{7}\right)^{t / 7}=\left(\frac{5}{4}\right)^{1}=1.25$, and so $\frac{t}{7} \log \frac{7.5}{7}=\log 1.25 \Rightarrow t=7 \log _{7.5} 1.25=7 \log _{7.5}(1 / 8)=7(-\log _{7.5} 8)=7(-\log _{7.5}(2^{3}))=-7(3 \log _{7.5} 2)=-7\left(\frac{\log _{2} 2}{\log _{2} 7.5}\right)(3)=-7\left(\frac{1}{\log _{2} 7.5}\right)(3)=-7\left(\frac{1}{\log _{2} 7.5}\right)(3)$. Now we can use a calculator to find $\log _{2} 7.5$, and we find that $\log _{2} 7.5 \approx 2.807354925$. Therefore, we have $t \approx-7\left(\frac{1}{2.807354925}\right)(3) \approx-7(0.353554218) \approx-2.469898152 \approx \boxed{2}$ days.
